Release 1.5.1

Changelog:
Release 1.5.1
    Python SDK:    1.5.1
        - coincides with C/C++ SDK 2024.11.26.2038
            - Added Apx60 CLC
            - IMX533/571 based cameras startup quicker whilst imaging
Release 1.5.0
    Python SDK:    1.5.0
        - added a new function (get_serial_str) that retrieves the serial number of a camera as a string
        - get_serial is depreceated in favour of get_serial_str
Release 1.4.1
    Python SDK:    1.4.1
        - coincides with C/C++ SDK 2024.08.30.1920
Release 1.4
    Python SDK:    1.4.0
        - added set_te_preview_gain_offset, get_te_preview_gain_offset, and get_te_preview_gain_offset functions
Release 1.3
    Python SDK:    1.3.0
        - added start_exposure, start_exposure_ms, image_ready, get_image functions
        - fixed issue with the output of the cooling flags return from the cooling_info function
Release 1.2
    Python SDK:    1.2.0
        - added get_te_readout_mode and set_te_readout_mode functions for the TE series cameras.
Release 1.1
    Python SDK:    1.1.0
        - added check_efw_moving
        - changed return type of efw_device_details
        - get_16bit_mode now returns SixteenBitMode enum name rather than int
Release 1.0
    Python SDK:    1.0.0
        - Full coverage of the C API.
Release 0.7
    Python SDK:    0.7.0
        - added get_firmware_version
        - added 16bit mode functions for ChemiMOS
        - added fast mode
Release 0.6 (C/C++ SDK 2021.11.16)
    Python SDK:    0.6.0
        - added has_pad_data 
        - added {set|get}_exposure_speed functionality that will work with our Horizon/ACIS/APX/TE cameras.
    Prerequisites: 0.5.0
        - fixed issue where the installer would try to install to SysWOW64 on a 64 bit system.
Release 0.5 (C/C++ SDK 2021.11.16)
    Python SDK:    0.5.0
        - set_gain_offset fixed
    Prerequisites: 0.4.0
Release 0.4
    Python SDK:    0.4.0
        - set_gain_offset fixed
    Prerequisites: 0.4.0
        - Updated to version 2021.11.16 of the C/C++ SDK (BETA).
Release 0.3
Release 0.2
    Python SDK:    0.2.0
        - Added the ability to set the gain and offset globally for all cameras via set_gain_offset() function
        - Added the ability to Pad Data (12bit -> 16bit) for our Horizon & ACIS series cameras
    Prerequisites: 0.2.0    
Release 0.1



